[b]A mod for Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord.[/b]

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

Keep your spare armour sets, your wife's dress and your best food away from the loot.

In your inventory, press [b]New chest[/b], give it a name, and put in what you want kept apart. A chest shows in your item list like any other goods; click it and it opens on the left, where you move things in and out.

What is in a chest is [b]out of your party's reach[/b]:
[list]
[*]never sold, not even by "sell all"
[*]never eaten
[*]never equipped by companions or used to upgrade troops
[*]never counted as trade goods
[/list]

It still [b]weighs what it holds[/b], so your party is as fast or as slow as before. Hover a chest to see what is inside, its weight and worth.

Chests open from your own inventory (the I key, on the map or in town). Up to 50 chests. Horses and other animals stay out.

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859188632]Harmony[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859222409]UIExtenderEx[/url]
[/list]
Works with or without War Sails. For Bannerlord v1.4.8.

Safe to add mid-campaign. [b]Before removing it, empty your chests:[/b] without the mod they turn into "Trash Item" and what was inside is gone.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Do whatever you like with it.
To thank me, open [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]my GitHub profile[/url] and read my top pinned.

Not on Steam? Download it from the [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/item-chests/releases/latest]GitHub Releases page[/url]. Source code and README: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/item-chests]github.com/TraxData313/item-chests[/url]
